# Changelog

The changelog records the main changes and improvements made to the Minelethu Baby Emporium website during each phase of the POE.


## Part 1 - Planning and HTML Development

### Initial Development

- Created the Minelethu Baby Emporium website proposal.
- Selected Minelethu Baby Emporium as the preferred website concept.
- Established MGM Holdings as the parent brand.
- Defined the website target audience as new and expecting parents, guardians and gift buyers.
- Created the website sitemap and basic wireframes.
- Created the initial GitHub repository and project folder structure.
- Created five HTML pages:
  - `index.html`
  - `about.html`
  - `products.html`
  - `enquiry.html`
  - `contact.html`
- Created the same navigation menu across all five pages.
- Added the Minelethu Baby Emporium business background.
- Added the mission, vision and values.
- Added the three main product categories:
  - Essential Baby Wear
  - Feeding and Nutrition Support
  - Sanitary and Hygiene Essentials
- Added product enquiry and general contact forms.
- Added the website footer and MGM Holdings branding.
- Added HTML comments to explain the main sections of the code.
- Tested the links between the five website pages.


## Part 2 - CSS and Responsive Design

### Styling and Visual Improvements

- Created an external stylesheet called `style.css`.
- Linked the same stylesheet to all five HTML pages.
- Added a CSS reset to create consistent spacing across the website.
- Added the Minelethu Baby Emporium colour palette:
  - Soft Sage `#A8BFA3`
  - Warm Cream `#FFF8EE`
  - Muted Peach `#E8A58D`
  - Dark Charcoal `#263238`
- Centred the main website headings, paragraphs, navigation and content.
- Styled the header and navigation menu.
- Added hover, focus and active states to navigation links and buttons.
- Added button styling for calls to action such as **Enquire Now** and **View Our Products**.
- Used CSS Grid to organise product and category cards.
- Used Flexbox for navigation and other website layout elements.
- Styled the About page, product cards, forms and footer.
- Added borders, rounded corners and box shadows to improve the visual design.
- Added product images for baby wear, feeding products and hygiene products.
- Added `alt` descriptions to product images to improve accessibility.
- Added responsive image styling.
- Added a tablet breakpoint at `900px`.
- Added a mobile breakpoint at `600px`.
- Changed product layouts from three columns on desktop to two columns on tablet and one column on mobile.
- Updated buttons and navigation for smaller screens.
- Tested the website layout across desktop, tablet and mobile screen sizes.


## Part 3 - JavaScript and Final Website Development

### JavaScript Functionality

- Created the external JavaScript file called `script.js`.
- Linked the JavaScript file to the website pages.
- Added JavaScript validation to the Product Enquiry form.
- Added validation for:
  - Required fields
  - Email addresses
  - Phone numbers
  - Product categories
  - Product quantities
  - Messages
  - Preferred contact methods
- Added JavaScript validation to the Contact form.
- Added success messages when forms pass validation.
- Added error messages when information is missing or incorrect.
- Added product search functionality to the Products page.
- Added product category filtering.
- Added `data-category` attributes to product cards to support filtering.
- Added JavaScript feedback areas to the Enquiry and Contact pages.


### SEO and Accessibility Improvements

- Added descriptive page titles to the HTML pages.
- Added meta descriptions to support basic SEO.
- Used a clear heading structure with `h1`, `h2` and `h3` headings.
- Added descriptive alternative text to website images.
- Used semantic HTML elements such as `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article` and `footer`.
- Used labels for form fields to improve accessibility.
- Used `aria-live` for JavaScript form feedback messages.


### Testing and Final Improvements

- Tested navigation between all five pages.
- Tested product links and Enquiry buttons.
- Tested the product search function.
- Tested the product category filter.
- Tested the Product Enquiry form validation.
- Tested the Contact form validation.
- Checked success and error messages.
- Checked images and image paths.
- Tested the website on desktop, tablet and mobile layouts.
- Checked that the website content matches the approved Minelethu Baby Emporium proposal.
- Updated the README file to reflect the final website development.

